From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: B Honey <bhoneycutt153@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: drm: send the CTM only when it changes

HwcDisplay passes the color matrix (the identity when nothing is set) with
every frame, and SetCtmIfNeeded() registered a new CTM blob for every
commit. The kernel marks a CRTC's color management as changed whenever its
CTM property gets a different blob, even one holding the same matrix.
amdgpu treats that as a reason to rebuild the CRTC's planes
(should_reset_plane: "CRTC Degamma changes currently require us to
recreate planes"), so every page flip became a full DC update. On DCN 3.5
(Radeon 890M, ASUS G14) a full update waits through the next vblank before
it programs the flip, so each flip landed two vblanks after its commit:
SurfaceFlinger at 120 Hz presented every 16.7 ms (TimeStats: 470 of 478
present intervals 16 ms, 477 of 480 frames missed, RenderEngine 3 ms), and
amdgpu never took its fast flip path (commit_planes_for_stream_fast: 0 of
61 commits).

Keep the last committed matrix in KmsState and leave the CRTC's blob alone
while the matrix is unchanged. A failed or test-only commit does not update
it, so the next commit sends the matrix again. The color-pipeline path
already sets 0 (no blob) and only clears the cache.
---
 drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++++
 drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.h   |  8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 23 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp b/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp
index 99d646f..a446b50 100644
--- a/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp
+++ b/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.cpp
@@ -317,9 +317,23 @@ bool DrmAtomicStateManager::SetCtmIfNeeded(const AtomicCommitArgs &args,
 
   auto *drm = pipe_->device;
   if (drm->GetResMan().UseColorPipeline()) {
+    request.new_frame_state.ctm.reset();
     return crtc->GetCtmProperty().AtomicSet(*request.property_set, 0);
   }
   auto drm_color_matrix = ColorUtil::ToColorTransform3x3(args.color_matrix);
+  if (!drm_color_matrix) {
+    ALOGE("Failed to convert the color matrix");
+    return false;
+  }
+
+  std::array<uint64_t, 9> matrix{};
+  std::copy(std::begin(drm_color_matrix->matrix),
+            std::end(drm_color_matrix->matrix), matrix.begin());
+  if (committed_frame_state_.ctm == matrix) {
+    /* Already on the CRTC: keep its blob (see KmsState::ctm). */
+    return true;
+  }
+
   auto ctm_blob = drm->RegisterUserPropertyBlob(drm_color_matrix.get(),
                                                 sizeof(drm_color_ctm));
   if (!ctm_blob) {
@@ -332,6 +346,7 @@ bool DrmAtomicStateManager::SetCtmIfNeeded(const AtomicCommitArgs &args,
   }
 
   request.used_kms_objects.blobs.emplace_back(std::move(ctm_blob));
+  request.new_frame_state.ctm = matrix;
   return true;
 }
 
diff --git a/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.h b/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.h
index 4e1eb9e..e003875 100644
--- a/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.h
+++ b/drm/DrmAtomicStateManager.h
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 
 #include <pthread.h>
 
+#include <array>
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <map>
 #include <memory>
@@ -75,6 +76,13 @@ class DrmAtomicStateManager : public DrmAtomicCommitSink {
 
     /* To avoid setting the inactive state twice, which will fail the commit */
     bool crtc_active_state{};
+
+    /* The CTM matrix last set on the CRTC. The kernel flags a color management
+     * change whenever the CTM property gets a new blob, even one with the same
+     * matrix, and amdgpu then rebuilds the planes: a full display update on every
+     * frame, so every flip misses a vblank. Unchanged matrices are not sent again.
+     */
+    std::optional<std::array<uint64_t, 9>> ctm;
   };
 
   // State for a pending atomic request. Includes the pending kms objects and
